## Empowering Inclusive Career Exploration

During the kickoff project in Digital Innovation (2DI), our entire cohort
collaborated on a socially impactful platform: a modernized **Work Interest
Test** for [MPI Oosterlo](https://www.mpi-oosterlo.be/).

The original tool had been utilized for years by MPI Oosterlo and roughly one
hundred other healthcare institutions across Flanders to gauge the vocational
interests of individuals with intellectual disabilities. Because the legacy
codebase (originally developed by applied psychology students in partnership
with the University of Volgograd) faced declining maintenance and support, we
were tasked with building a modern, reliable, and easily maintainable
replacement.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## How the Assessment Works

The core philosophy of the application is providing an accessible, objective
foundation for exploratory conversations between clients and their counselors:

* **Visual Work Scenarios**: Clients are presented with curated media showcasing
  various vocational activities and workplace settings.
* **Intuitive 3-State Interaction**:
  * 🟢 **Green**: *"I want to do this"*
  * 🔴 **Red**: *"I don't want to do this"*
  * ➡️ **Arrow**: *"Ignore this photo / No preference"*
* **Dialogue Catalyst**: The resulting interest profile serves as a concrete
  starting point for mentors and job coaches to plan personalized guidance.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Key Features & Architecture

### 1. Privacy & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

* Structured separation between **Institution Administrators**,
  **Mentors/Counselors**, and **Clients**.
* Privacy-first data isolation: individual client results are strictly
  confidential and accessible solely by their assigned mentor, while anonymized
  aggregate metrics can be leveraged for administrative analytics.

### 2. Multi-Format Media & Accessibility

* Flexible media handling: supports static photography, animated GIFs, YouTube
  video embeds, and audio clips to accommodate diverse cognitive and sensory
  needs.
* **Multilingual Assessment**: The client-facing test runner supports multiple
  languages, ensuring individuals from diverse linguistic backgrounds can
  complete it comfortably.

### 3. Dynamic Test & Asset Management

* Administrators can dynamically configure custom tests, group items into
  categories, and manage media libraries directly through the admin panel.

### 4. Response Analysis

* **Response Latency Tracking**: Records the time taken per question,
  highlighting hesitation patterns that help mentors identify topics needing
  deeper discussion.

### 5. Data Intelligence & BI Capabilities

* Seamless migration and integration of multi-year historical assessment data.
* Architected for integration with Business Intelligence (BI) dashboards to
  support strategic decision-making regarding employment trends at regional and
  national levels.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Collaborative Teamwork

As the kickoff project for DI, this was both a technical challenge and a
team-building journey for our entire student cohort. Over the course of six
weeks, we discovered each other's strengths across project analysis, UI design,
frontend engineering, and backend architecture, delivering a production-ready
application.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Technology Stack

* **Backend & Framework**: PHP & Laravel
* **Reactivity**: Livewire & Alpine.js
* **Styling**: Tailwind CSS
* **Database**: MariaDB
* **Analysis & Design**: Project Analysis, UI/UX Design with Figma & UML

